    },
    "body": "References #421. First end-to-end measurement of the original hybrid: router-selected anchors feeding the infill engine. Natural stack, 2000/200 story caps, pre-declared exit rule. **ARM A true 31.5% free top-1 (ceiling) | ARM B router 7.6% | ARM C unigram 2.1% | ARM D shuffled-router 3.1%. B beats C by +5.5pp (needed ≥2) and beats D by +4.55pp (needed >0) → POSITIVE.** Also confirms the #273 claim: routed beats shuffled — routing carries positional information. Honest limitations in the harness docs: oracle query context (upper bound), synthetic-word token mapping, cosine-core retrieval.",
